as in charge  however the primordial is quite  deceptive as it was able to convince  mendican bias to side with him which  caused the primordial to break out of  containment releasing all the flood on  the halo ring lots of other small  details occurred between now and then as  that was almost a hundred thousand years  ago however what's more important is  that to anyone's knowledge mendican bias  and the primordial may still very well  be alive and on this ring as for the  banish they were introduced in halo wars  2. they're a mercenary faction that  split off from the original covenant  empire they're sort of like joel  madame's covenant which was a splinter  group form from some of the covenant's  original soldiers except they differ in  a few ideologies the banished are led by  warmaster atriox and are primarily  composed of brutes however they do have  other species within their ranks they're  a group that is all about power  constantly throughout the game esheram  will try to challenge us as they crave  the hunt killing and hunting stronger  foes to prove that they're powerful is  what they do its four most important  members are atriox decimus asheram and  jega the blademaster decimus was killed  in halo wars 2 and since he was second  in command within the banish the  runner-up would take his place which was  esherum we already know about atriox and  esherum from just the few missions in  game but the only outlier of the group  is jega probably the coolest character  in the entire game as he has earned the  title of spartan killer all of them  minus decimates are the main characters  of the banished and halo infinite and  will constantly appear throughout the  game to continue back to where we left  off originally i was going to explain  the rest of the story chronologically  from the game's point of view but then  that got too convoluted so i'll try to  establish an actual timeline of events  there's been quite a lot of time between  halo 5 and halo infinite if i'm not  mistaken it's been about three years  since then so cortana has had a lot of  time to plan her attacks throughout the  game the chief will hear whispers and  see echoes of cortana these are assumed  to be fragments of her memories that the  chief can somehow see we first see  cortana talking to an ai called leonidas  he was in charge of laconia station and  was allied with cortana she orders him  to sacrifice himself and leonidas  self-destructs killing all the unsc  soldiers and spartans on board the next  one is her talking with lord hood from  halo 3 about earth's surrender even the  homeworld of the unsc isn't safe from  her jurisdiction to provoke them she  even summoned her guardian who was  waiting to fire in case things didn't go  her way according to the master chief he  witnessed the guardian completely  eliminate sydney australia so it seems  that lord hood was not budging on her  offer the final echo we see is her  talking with atriox where she goes one  step further and threatens the entire  banished homeworld atriox of course  refuses to align himself with her and  the entire planet of dossier is  completely destroyed in front of his  eyes cortana has gone completely mad  with power and is not willing to listen  to anyone as we enter the final mission  we get even more echoes but this being  about her and atriox the first echo we  see we hear cortana talking about  waiting for a specific person to show up  and asking what that plan is questioning  what halsey will think if they try to  destroy her she thought the person that  walked into the room was chief however  it was actually atriox once again to  provide more context throughout the game  we get a few bits here and there about  what's going on with the weapon  essentially in between the events of  halo 5 and halo infinite the master  chief was tasked with the deletion of  cortana he had witnessed the destruction  on earth and all the other planets he  destroyed and realized that it w