rolling the ring and  subsequently firing that ring the  banished are trying to activate the  spires on the ring as the spire's main  jobs are to rebuild the parts of the  ring that have been destroyed the only  way for the chief to prevent them from  firing this ring is with the help of the  weapon our previous information explains  why he knows of the weapon's existence  and where it's located as he was tasked  with helping her delete cortana the  master chief meets with the weapon and  asks where cortana is she says that  cortana has already been deleted at the  moment the two don't know why but once  again previous info i've already talked  about explains why as she sacrificed  herself to blow up zeta halo so keep in  mind that two storylines are going on we  have the war against the banished and  cortana the chief is doing both at the  same time so things can get a little bit  intertwined most of the missions for now  are just about defeating the banished  and taking back the ring but eventually  we'll discover a banished dig site upon  entering this dig site we meet a monitor  named despondent pyre she's freaking out  currently as something called the  harbinger is awake and judging by her  tone this doesn't sound like a good  thing when we make our way through the  conservatory we hear despondent empire  being interrogated by this harbinger and  she talks about reviving the endless we  find her separated into multiple pieces  and we also get to see an echo of  cortana and despondent pyre pyre  explains that cortana may have the  weapons of the halo ring but its secrets  it holds can never be unearthed cortana  believes that pyre is talking about the  flood and explains to her that there are  more things dangerous on this ring than  the flood this is extremely terrifying  in so many different ways not only does  this confirm to us that the flood were  or possibly still are on this ring but  something far worse exists here seeing  as within this whole franchise