as time  to come to terms with reality cortana is  not the same cortana he once knew as  that one died in halo 4 and this new one  is one that seeks vengeance so despite  their relationship together he wanted to  see his mission through dr halsey then  created another ai who we know as the  weapon her task was to mimic the  original cortana so that she could be  lured onto zeta halo and be trapped  there after being trapped cortana would  then be deleted and so would the weapon  as she served her purpose which was to  capture cortana however while the weapon  succeeded in trapping cortana the chiefs  did not get to her first as atriox beat  him to her going back to the echo we see  that atriox and cortana meet together  atriox says that cortana's empire is  over and that he's here to discuss her  terms of surrender atriax goes on to  explain that he has discovered immense  power within this ring and what the  silent auditorium truly is he wants  cortana to relinquish control of the  ring as that's all atriox wants with the  power of the halo ring underneath  banished control they could wipe out  galaxies without even trying so cortana  devised a plan and ends up blowing up  the halo ring with the ring broken it  can no longer fire preventing atriox and  the bandish from claiming it as their  own from what we can gather shortly  after this it seems that cortana  sacrificed herself to blow up the ring  not the halo 4 split into fragments then  become an immortal sacrifice i mean this  time she seems truly dead this explains  how cortana the weapon and atriox got  here and why the ring is destroyed with  that out of the way we can fast forward  to present day towards the end of the  first mission we discover that atriox is  dead we have no clue how or when we just  know that he died this is completely  untrue but once again more on that later  the master chief with the help of the  pilot lands on zeta halo as he has one  mission in mind stopping the banished  from controlling the ring and  subsequently firing that ring the  banished are trying to activate the  spires on the ring as the spire's main  jobs are to rebuild the parts of the  ring that have been destroyed the only  way for the chief to prevent them from  firing this ring is with the help of the  weapon our previous information explains  why he knows of the weapon's existence  and where it's located as he was tasked  with helping her delete cortana the  master chief meets with the weapon and  asks where cortana is she says that  cortana has already been deleted at the  moment the two don't know why but once  again previous info i've already talked  about explains why as she sacrificed  herself to blow up zeta halo so keep in  mind that two storylines are going on we  have the war against the banished and  cortana the chief is doing both at the  same time so things can get a little bit  intertwined most of the missions for now  are just about defeating the banished  and taking back the ring but eventually  we'll discover a banished dig site upon  entering this dig site we meet a monitor  named despondent pyre she's freaking out  currently as something called the  harbinger is awake and judging by her  tone this doesn't sound like a good  thing when we make our way through the  conservatory we hear despondent empire  being interrogated by this harbinger and  she talks about reviving the endless we  find her separated into multiple pieces  and we also get to see an echo of  cortana and despondent pyre pyre  explains that cortana may have the  weapons of the halo ring but its secrets  it holds can never be unearthed cortana  believes that pyre is talking about the  flood and explains to her that there are  more things dangerous on this ring than  the flood this is extremely terrifying  in so many different ways not only does  this confirm to us that the flood were  or possibly still are on this ring but  something far worse exists here seeing  as within this whole franchise the flood  has always been the strongest and most  terrifying force to go up against the  fact that there's something even worse  is a bit bone chilling pyre is freaking  out and trying to explain to cortana  that the punish must not be freed but  cortana refuses to listen this possibly  explains how the harbinger was able to  be awoken we eventually come face to  face with said harbinger and it's quite  clear that she is of a very different  species something we haven't seen before  the harbinger says that the forerunner's  lies are at an end and the endless will  be found justo talks about something  called the reformation after this the  chief then learns of the spires and  heads to one to take it down it's here  where we meet agitant resolution he's a  sub-monitor that was created to replace  the spawn empire should she be  decommissioned or destroyed just like  the guilty spark he doesn't take too  kindly to having his spire be destroyed  so he attacks us on sight the chief  defeats him and the spire is shut down  except only one of them is shut down  there are still 10 more spires to hunt  down but one of them has the control  room within it this is kind of like how  each halo ring can be fired separately  but can also be fired all at once from  the ark but instead of rings it's these  spires before we destroy it we get a  cutscene between the harbinger and  escheram atrox apparently found the  harbinger sometime during his travels  and decided to work together the  harbinger just wants to bring back the  endless she's fine with the banish  taking the ring so as long as each party  gets their goals met they won't meddle  in each other's affairs however this  alliance is very shaky as the two  definitely don't trust one another back  to the chief he had the weapon make it  through the 4runner structure to shut  down the spire however one of these  instances is very important throughout  this mission the weapon claims to have  been scanned by something that is being  watched by someone as a precaution  master chief seems to be doing something  with his suits software minutes later  when they get inside the control room  the weapon attempts to finish the  process but the harbinger stops the  weapon chief uses this exact same  software program that he did earlier if  you read the text that appears during  this he was trying to delete the weapon  in case she was caught or taken this  goes back to what the weapon said  earlier in that mission about wanting  the chief to trust her glee he doesn't  trust her at all as he almost deleted  her at the first sign of danger  something he would never do with cortana  this causes some discrepancy between the  two as the weapon trusts the chief and  is willing to do what he needs her to do  but despite all she's done to help he  still won't trust her because of this  encounter though the harbinger was able  to start the reformation process this  reformation is taking place at the  silent auditorium the area we were in  when we were talking about those echoes  with cortana and atriox before we can  leave we get another boss fight with the  sub monitor who is trying to kill us so  the harbinger can start the reformation  process it does come out eventually that  he was wrong as he didn't understand  what the reformation was but at this  moment he is still trying to kill us  afterwards the pilot comes to pick us up  until he's attacked and captured by jega  we've already seen jaeger's work in  action as he's killed all the sparrings  we take the abilities from but now he  wants to kill us and he's luring us into  a trap by using the pilot as bait the  master chief being the master chief of  course goes after the pilot and has to  go through the house of reckoning it's  an arena built by the banish so they can  hunt the unsc members they capture by  giving them weapons and a base to defend  themselves while the banished attack  them from all angles it's quite the sick  and twisted game after making it through  the basic and advanced version of the  arena we get into probably the toughest  part of the game as now we have to  defeat jega the room is dark with tight  spaces and very little room to breathe  jega also uses an energy sword and  active camo making this fight incredibly  terrifying after defeating jega we walk  10 feet out of the room and get into  another boss fight with escheram who is  also insanely tough but of course he's  the master chief so he'll prevail and  rescue the pilot the three then go to  the silent auditorium to stop the  harbinger this journey also ties into a  discovery that the weapon is cortana yes  she dresses and sounds like her but it's  not a coincidence she is a literal copy  of her in halo 4 cortana talks about  being replaced with another ai after  she's dead possibly even one that looks  like her well they weren't kidding as  the weapon is literally cortana just  without the knowledge of their  adventures she's basically pre-halo 1  cortana who only knew of the chief's  existence and nothing else the weapon is  clearly worried is now that she realizes  she's a copy of cortana she's worried  that she'll go rampant too but that's  also another mission the master chief  was tasked with preventing her from  being another cortana continuing into  the silent auditorium we make it to  where cortana sacrificed herself and  then meet the harbinger according to the  harbinger the place we're stepping foot  in is where the forerunners pass  judgment on the harbinger in her kind it  seems that she has some hatred towards  the forerunners because of what they did  to her and the endless which is why  she's trying to revive them we do  eventually stop her but before she dies  she mentions that while her time is up  and that she's been defeated the chief  in the weapons time is up too as it  seems like she was able to contact the  endless before her death right after  this we get another echo of cortana but  this one's a little different it doesn't  seem like a memory more like a planned  message for the chief and the weapon she  says her goodbyes but wants to apologize  for what she's done she admits that she  was wrong and that the entire reason  they're together was because they were a  team and her going off on her own was  stupid of her to do that cortana wants  the chief and the weapon to learn from  her mistakes and to not repeat them  again the two then escape the silent  auditorium together and reunite with the  pilot there's also this sweet moment  where the group exchanged names and we  discover that the pilot's name is  fernando fernando then asked the weapon  what to call her and judging from the  fact that she asked the chief for  permission it sounds like she's gonna be  going with cortana as her name the three  then discuss future plans as it becomes  clear to all three of them that the ring  houses something more dangerous plus the  banish still controls zeta halo so their  work isn't finished however while their  work is only beginning ours is done as  we reach the end of the campaign we do  get a post-credit cutscene which shows  atriox who is not actually dead  activating this device which opens a  room with a ton of forerunner slabs all  with a unique marking on it from what we  can gather from these endings i do have  some theories firstly the harbinger  talks about the endless this is either  the name of her species or the name of  the faction my first choice is a species  however there is an audio log from  despondent pyre that talks about an  uncatalogued species called the xalanine  my actual theory though is that the  harbinger is related to the precursors  and seeing as this endless group is  probably going to be our next threat  that means that we will finally be able  to see the precursors in game for the  first time with the post-credit cutscene  in mind it seems that atriox will  definitely play a large role in the next  story as he seems to have his own  motivations if any or all of this is  true this next game is going to be  insane but now we've officially come to  the end of the game and we've also come  to the end of the video thank you all  for watching today and hopefully i was  able to convey the story well enough to  you if you have any questions leave them  down below and i can maybe try to help  you regardless thank you for making it  this far in the video do let me know  your thoughts on the campaign and the  ending as a whole i'll be saving my  thoughts for that future review on the  campaign so look forward to that to hold  you over though don't forget to check  out my halo series retrospective video  as a lot of you seem to love it so thank  you all for the support on that with out  of the way like the video if you enjoyed  it subscribe if you're new and as always  thank you to my returning viewers for  coming back  take care everyone  goodbye  [Music]  you
 

